{"id": "EUVD-2026-67557", "enisaUuid": "453ddacb-b5e2-37f2-b087-4349c5660d9b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: re-fetch eth header after route_shortcircuit()\n\nBefore route_shortcircuit(), the eth header pointer is cached from eth_hdr(skb).\n\nInside route_shortcircuit(), pskb_may_pull() can be called, which may\nreallocate skb->head.\n\nIn this case, returning to vxlan_xmit() leaves the cached eth pointer pointing to\nfreed memory, leading to a use-after-free when dereferencing eth->h_dest.\n\nFix this by updating eth = eth_hdr(skb) after calling route_shortcircuit().", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:52:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:32", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6375093eb45cd7d89f1945f939eeae3b29d79f56", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b7f7b653e3557690047c62f03b80a24ea5a58a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf045341dfb3e767f0ff94cf240ce3c371973bd4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2355c8c26d2aa1b4385b369e67202e47d460d555", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1511631b7cfc4152b10a0a9d04c7a0bf2ddf4585", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1235e017aa11cf01e91b613c4c5ed6aa28934fff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9dceac9e1c7c772c43c732fc0d325e72835801a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1395a676ec15a0a02a2a6d86602324f2d5fd41d5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80681", "GHSA-6mmh-5qqr-f237"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a20595e-f26e-3fd7-ab5f-37e3f00aaa0a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae8840825605f36f98f247323edc150e761cb64e <1235e017aa11cf01e91b613c4c5ed6aa28934fff"}, {"id": "0fde84f9-cc6e-3dfd-8f2e-1655793e68ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "1d90df6f-fd96-3144-9b44-df91e3cd557e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendo